  "description": "ComputeSpansForRectangle as a scan conversion (TR7). The corners are p0 = (a, e), p1 = (a, -e), p2 = (-a, -e), p3 = (-a, e) rotated by (cos, sin) about the centre, a = -w/2, e = -h/2. Each row z in zMin..zMax (truncated corner rows, zMin >= 0, zMax clamped unsigned to cellsZ) takes the edges that cross 16z half-open, the crossing column trunc(trunc(x) / 16); start = the minimum (>= 0), end = the maximum + 1 (clamped unsigned to cellsX); a row no edge crosses has start = INT_MAX and is empty. The worked example (sinkhole, angle 0, 16 x 16 m at (160, 160)): rows 9 (empty) and 10 (9..11), so the sinkhole touches only vertex (10, 10). A 64 m square turned by 45 degrees: the spans follow the crossing columns (8: 9..11, 9: 8..12, 10: 7..13, 11: 8..12, 12: 9..11), not the bounding box 7..13. Clamps at the low corner (start 0) and past the high side (end 20, rows to 20).",
